.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH SPT-FORWARD 1  "forward " 
.SH NAME
forward \- Manage forwards (local/remote TCP, UDP)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBforward\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage forwards (local/remote TCP, UDP)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
forward\-list(1)
List configured forwards
.TP
forward\-show(1)
Show a forward
.TP
forward\-add(1)
Add a forward
.TP
forward\-explain(1)
Explain how a forward is plumbed
.TP
forward\-test(1)
Run targeted forward tests
.TP
forward\-throttle(1)
Update throttle/limit knobs at runtime
.TP
forward\-remove(1)
Remove a forward
.TP
forward\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  spt forward add local \-\-profile edge \-\-listen 127.0.0.1:5432 \-\-to db:5432 \-\-tcp
  spt forward add remote \-\-profile edge \-\-listen 0.0.0.0:8080 \-\-to web:80 \-\-tcp
  spt forward throttle edge/db \-\-in 10MiB/s \-\-out 10MiB/s \-\-connections 64
  spt forward test edge/db \-\-connect \-\-dns\-name db.local
  spt forward remove edge/db
